Third-party media libraries bundled with Kube Workspaces (Tier 1 decode)
=============================================================================

This software uses code of FFmpeg licensed under the LGPLv2.1, and the Opus
reference implementation under the 3-clause BSD license. Exact source
versions, build flags and hashes are pinned in third_party/media-libs/MANIFEST
in the desktop-client source tree; per-target configure lines are recorded in
each package's BUILD-INFO-ffmpeg.txt / BUILD-INFO-opus.txt.

FFmpeg 5.1.x (libavcodec 59 / libavutil 57)
  Source: https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ (see MANIFEST for the pinned file+hash)
  License: GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 or later (LGPLv2.1+).
  The bundled build is configured WITHOUT --enable-gpl, --enable-nonfree or
  --enable-version3 (decoder-only: H.264 decode; no x264/x265). Full license
  text ships beside the binaries as COPYING.LGPLv2.1. Corresponding source is
  the pinned release tarball above; build scripts are in the source tree.
  The libraries are loaded dynamically at runtime and remain replaceable with
  any ABI-compatible build (drop-in beside the executable).

Opus (libopus)
  Source: https://downloads.xiph.org/releases/opus/ (see MANIFEST)
  License: 3-clause BSD (copyright Xiph.Org et al.; full text ships as
  COPYING.opus-BSD). Royalty-free patent grants apply per opus-codec.org/license.
  Binary redistribution reproduces that notice here and in that file.

Kube Workspaces itself is Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE). Nothing above relicenses
it: both libraries are used through dynamic loading under their own terms.
